<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rajputs</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Rajput</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Rajputs are a group of warrior clans of northern and western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, many of whom ruled kingdoms in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasthan">Rajasthan</a> and neighbouring regions. They resisted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate</a> and the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughal Empire</a>, as at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-khanwa">Battle of Khanwa</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babur">Babur</a> in 1527, but many later became Mughal allies. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha Empire</a> also imposed tribute arrangements on Rajput states.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rajputs.jpg" alt="Rajputs" width="216" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Raja Ravi Varma · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ravi_Varma-Rajput_soldier.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
